From 17011f84fbf0964cf6362a0dbf091c4c0a5184aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:57:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] [DASH] Compare a segment end with the period end on the
 same time line

In a live stream, AdaptiveTree::IsLastSegment compares the end of a
segment with the end of a period that is not the last. The period end is
on the time line of the period starts, but DASH segment times are not
always on that time line:

- SegmentList times start at 0 in each period.
- SegmentTimeline times with a presentationTimeOffset are media times,
  and the offset is the media time of the period start.

So a complete period whose segment times were below the period end never
ended: ensureSegment waited for segments that no update adds. A period
still in progress whose segment times were above the period end ended
too early, and the stream continued at the next period.

CDashTree::GetSegmentEndMs now converts the segment end to the time line
of the period starts. The times of a SegmentTemplate duration, of a
SegmentTimeline without an offset, and of a SegmentBase index already
are on that time line.

DASHTreeTest.LastSegmentOfEachPeriod runs the real AdaptiveStream over
each segment source, with live and VOD, offsets above and below the
period start, periods in progress, and each update mode, also a live
manifest without updates, where no segment follows the timeline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
